Subject: winebus: show a DualSense as a DualShock 4 or an Xbox 360 controller on request.
Author: AnvilMac contributors (Claude Code), 2026-10-29
Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, same as Wine dlls/winebus.sys/bus_iohid.c.
Provenance: original change against Wine 11.19 with AnvilMac patch 0011, source tarball
73eb0b02dfc0cb0ff4f4d8d36c5786261e9725ac91968ae4d4e4b9a498c4087f.
Not an upstream commit; not submitted upstream.

Games whose own controller code predates the DualSense (Rewired before 1.1.38,
e.g. Unruly Heroes) see it but map no buttons. WINEBUS_DUALSENSE, set per game
by AnvilMac, changes how a DualSense (054c:0ce6, USB or Bluetooth) is shown to Windows:

  ds4:  as a DualShock 4 (054c:09cc, "Wireless Controller"), with a DualShock 4
        USB report descriptor; input reports rewritten to the DualShock 4
        layout; DualShock 4 output report 5 (rumble, light bar) sent to the
        DualSense as output report 2; feature reports refused.
  xbox: as an Xbox 360 controller (045e:028e, XInput through winexinput),
        using Wine's hid_device_add_gamepad layout and haptics, filled from
        the DualSense's reports, rumble sent back to it. is_hidraw follows
        winebus.sys's preference rule so the device is kept.

Over Bluetooth the modes request feature report 5 (calibration) at device start,
which makes the pad send its full report 0x31, read its input in the USB layout
(0x31 without its extra byte; the short report 1 as a fallback), and send output
as Bluetooth report 0x31 with its CRC-32 (seed 0xa2). The DualShock 4 shape is
presented as a USB pad, so the DualShock 4 Bluetooth handling doesn't apply to it.

Unset (or any other value): unchanged, over USB and Bluetooth.

Tested 2026-10-29 with a local build of this code on 11.19-10 and the owner's
pad: by USB, Unruly Heroes worked as ds4 (PlayStation icons; output report 5
translated) and as xbox (Xbox icons, XInput, rumble), Shank as xbox; over
Bluetooth, Unruly Heroes as ds4 and as xbox, Shank as itself (and with SDL,
patch 0013, present).

Protocol references (consulted 2026-10-29): Linux drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c
(DualSense input/output report layout, Bluetooth CRC), Linux drivers/hid/hid-sony.c and
SDL src/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_ps4.c (DualShock 4 USB layout). No code copied.
